# oracle: w311gneb_lbfgs — w194gneb_chain with min_style spin/lbfgs: the multireplica branch of MinSpinLBFGS (the two-loop recursion and the maximum rotation summed over all replicas, the end replicas fixed)
# oracle-partitions: 4
# oracle-inputs: w194gneb_chain.data w194gneb_chain.final
# oracle-compare: rel=5e-8 abs=1e-10 printed=8
# Measured with native LAMMPS: the 14 table rows agree at the printed precision; unrounded, the largest difference is 4.2e-8 (RDT), the printed digits themselves (rel 5e-8: one value sits on a rounding boundary of the 8th digit). With the earlier rounded hbar (6.5821191e-4) the table left native's from iteration 59 on and reached 1.3e-4.
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style spin
atom_modify map array
read_data w194gneb_chain.data
mass 1 55.845
pair_style spin/exchange 3.0
pair_coeff * * exchange 3.0 0.02726 0.2171 1.841
neighbor 0.1 bin
neigh_modify every 10 check yes delay 20
fix 1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.1 0.0 0.0 1.0 anisotropy 0.0001 1.0 0.0 0.0
fix_modify 1 energy yes
fix 3 all neb/spin 1.0
timestep 0.0001
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g
min_style spin/lbfgs
min_modify line spin_none discrete_factor 10.0
neb/spin 0.0 0.0 60 60 10 final w194gneb_chain.final
